  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Hippurin-1 and DO4 through a series of target interactions. Hippurin-1 is implicated in targeting VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Myxotyroside B and also of (7S,11S)-(+)-12-acetoxysydonic acid, both of which have a target relationship with DO4. Similarly, Hippurin-1 is also linked to Calenduloside C, which targets DO4. These findings collectively indicate that Hippurin-1 may act as a modulator or inhibitor of a pathway that ultimately leads to DO4 as a downstream target. The scores from the different paths suggest a consistent pattern of interaction, though the exact nature of the relationship remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a possible functional link between Hippurin-1 and DO4, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the mechanistic details.",
